    {
      "id": "p0092-b014",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The localization team hoped to find a fitting Japanese retro game quote for Loox’s battle message. After some time, though, the team decided to prioritize the line’s functional purpose over its decorative purpose. Thus, Loox still says “please don’t pick on me” in Japanese, but only as a simple, straightforward statement.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.2852467,
          0.8114286,
          0.9117707,
          0.905
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2852467,
          0.8114286,
          0.9117707,
          0.905
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "本地化团队本想找一句合适的日本老游戏台词，作为 Loox 的战斗发言。但斟酌一番后，团队决定优先保留这句话的实际作用，而不是它作为典故的点缀作用。因此，日版的 Loox 依然会说“请别欺负我”，只是变成了一句平实、直接的话。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.2944153,
          0.81,
          0.9087145,
          0.9135714
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "line_height": 1.45,
        "font_weight": 450,
        "background": "transparent",
        "text_align": "justify"
      },
      "notes": "原图与截图保留；译文为待审校初稿。",
      "calibration": {
